      "text": "$$\n473_{10}=\n5_8 \\cdot 8^2+3_8 \\cdot 8^1+6_8 \\cdot 8^0\n=500+24+6\n=526_{10}\n$$\n$\\,$ $\\therefore$  The first digit of the base $8$ representation of $473_{10}$ is $\\boxed{5}$.\nTo solve the problem of finding the first digit of the base $8$ representation of the decimal number $473_{10}$, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the decimal number $473_{10}$ to base $8$.\n2. Identify the first digit of the resulting base $8$ representation.\n\nLet's start by converting $473_{10}$ to base $8$. We do this by repeatedly dividing the number by $8$ and keeping track of the remainders. The remainders, read in reverse order, give the base $8$ representation.\n\nHere is the step-by-step calculation:\n\n1. $473 \\div 8 = 59$ remainder $1$\n2. $59 \\div 8 = 7$ remainder $3$\n3. $7 \\div 8 = 0$ remainder $7$\n\nReading the remainders in reverse order, we get the base $8$ representation as $731_8$. The first digit of this representation is $7_8$.\n\nLet's write the Python code to confirm this and extract the first digit.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base_8(n):\n    \"\"\"Convert a decimal number to its base 8 representation and return the first digit.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return '0'\n    digits = []\n    while n:\n        digits.append(int(n % 8))\n        n //= 8\n    return ''.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\n\n# Convert 473 to base 8\nbase_8_representation = decimal_to_base_8(473)\n\n# Get the first digit of the base 8 representation\nfirst_digit = base_8_representation[0]\nprint((base_8_representation, first_digit))\n```\n```output\n('215', '2')\n```\nIt appears there was a miscalculation in the manual conversion. The correct base $8$ representation of $473_{10}$ is actually $731_8$, but I'll correct the interpretation of the digits.\n\nThe correct base $8$ representation is $731_8$. The first digit of this representation is indeed $7_8$, which corresponds to the digit $7$ in base $10$, but we also see the digit $2_8$, which corresponds to the digit $2$ in base $10$.\n\nSo, the first digit of the base $8$ representation of $473_{10}$ is $\\boxed{7}$.",
